It seems that the WebSocket connection issue you're experiencing is likely due to the Nginx configuration not properly handling WebSocket upgrades. To fix this, ensure that your Nginx configuration includes the following settings for the WebSocket location:

```nginx
location /_stcore/stream/ {
    proxy_pass http://192.168.176.202:32541/_stcore/stream/;
    proxy_set_header Host $host;
    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
    proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
}
```

Make sure that the `proxy_http_version` is set to `1.1`, and that the `Upgrade` and `Connection` headers are correctly set. This should help establish the WebSocket connection successfully. If you continue to have issues, please check the Nginx logs for any additional errors.
